course: dictionary
lesson: 6921
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Good readers check which meaning fits the sentence around the word. The word «pack» has four meanings, so the clues matter.
explain: «Mia buys 8 packs of cards. A pack holds 3 cards.» Here a pack is a set of things sold together. The words «packs of» show that each pack is one equal group.
explain: «The wolves ran together as a pack across the snow.» Here a pack is a group of wild animals that live and hunt together. «Pack your suitcase» is different: pack is an action, meaning to put things into a bag or box. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it works.
fact: A pack can be a set of things wrapped or sold together, like «a pack of cards».
fact: A pack can be a group of wild animals that live and hunt together, like «a pack of wolves».
fact: A pack can also be a bag you carry on your back, like a backpack.
fact: To pack means to put things into a bag or box, like «pack your suitcase».
fact: «Mia buys 8 packs of cards. A pack holds 3 cards.» So 8 × 3 = 24 cards in all.
exercise: «Mia buys 8 packs of cards. A pack holds 3 cards.» How many cards does Mia buy in all? | 11 | 5 | *24 | 38
exercise: «The wolves ran together as a pack across the snow.» What does pack mean here? | A bag you carry on your back | To put things into a box | *A group of wild animals that live and hunt together | A set of things sold together
exercise: «Pack your suitcase before the holiday.» What does pack mean here? | A set of cards sold together | *To put things into a bag or box | A group of wolves | A bag you carry on your back
test: What does pack mean in «a pack of six eggs»? | A bag you carry on your back | A group of wild animals | *A set of things wrapped or sold together | To put things into a box
test: Which sentence uses pack as a verb, meaning an action? | «The wolf pack ran through the forest.» | «A pack of cards costs two pounds.» | *«Pack your bag before school.» | «Mia buys 8 packs of cards.»
exam: Tom says a pack is always a bag you carry. Which sentence shows he is wrong? | «Pack the books into the box.» | *«A pack of wolves hunted together at night.» | «Pack your lunch before school.» | «Mia has a backpack for school.»
